            <ArticleTitle>Classifying asthma severity: prospective symptom diary or retrospective symptom recall?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>537-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We used an observational within-subject control study at an inner-city school to compare asthma severity classification obtained by retrospective symptom recall with that obtained by a prospective symptom diary. The prospective symptom diary identified a higher proportion of persistent asthmatics than the retrospective symptom recall.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
